# p_d3a9 — Minimal travel: Hana only takes keys and wallet; laptop stays home

Hana works from home most of the time or has a very light commute. She only takes her keys and wallet out (to the mail box, a nearby café, a short walk). Her laptop, charger, handbag, jacket, hat, sunglasses, pen, and water bottle all stay in the house. The laptop is at desk_b1 from 8:00 to 17:30 on weekdays (she works from the desk). Priya follows the standard pattern: walk 7:30–9:00, errands 14:00–16:00 on weekdays; weekend walk 10–12. The guitar stays in the bedroom. The book stays on the nightstand.

What sets this hypothesis apart: Hana's laptop is NEVER out of the house. Her charger, handbag, jacket, hat, sunglasses, pen, and water bottle are always in the house. The entry hook retains all her items throughout the day. What would refute it: laptop_hana sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE at any time, or charger_hana missing from the house on a weekday between 9:00 and 17:00.

